## 1. Introduction

The Personal Finance Advisor Bot is an AI-assisted web application designed to help users manage their personal finances efficiently. It helps users track income and expenses, prepare budgets, analyze spending patterns, identify potential savings opportunities, and receive financial planning suggestions.

The application uses Python and Flask for its backend, SQLAlchemy for database operations, and SQLite for local data storage. It can integrate with Google's Gemini AI to generate financial insights. The application also supports rule-based fallback logic for selected features when AI services are unavailable.

## 2. Problem Statement

Managing personal finances can be challenging because people often struggle to track daily expenses, control unnecessary spending, plan monthly budgets, and achieve savings goals.

Traditional manual tracking methods can be time-consuming and make it difficult to identify spending patterns.

Therefore, a digital solution is needed to organize financial information, simplify budgeting, and provide useful insights that help users make informed financial decisions.

## 3. Objectives

The main objectives of the Personal Finance Advisor Bot are:

1. To track users' income and expenses.
2. To categorize expenses for easier financial analysis.
3. To generate personalized budget suggestions.
4. To identify spending patterns and possible savings opportunities.
5. To support savings goals and financial planning.
6. To generate monthly financial summaries and reports.
7. To use AI-assisted analysis to provide financial guidance.
8. To maintain financial records using a database.
9. To provide fallback functionality when AI services are unavailable.

## 4. Scope of the Project

The application focuses on personal financial organization and budgeting. Users can enter their income, expenses, and financial goals to receive a summarized view of their financial situation.

The project can be used by students, employees, and individuals who want to improve their budgeting habits.

The current project is intended as a financial planning aid. Integration with actual bank accounts, advanced investment analysis, and other financial services would require additional development.

## 5. Main Features

### 5.1 Income Tracking
Users can enter their income to establish a basis for budget planning.

### 5.2 Expense Management
Users can record expenses and organize them into categories such as rent, food, transportation, utilities, entertainment, and dining.

### 5.3 Budget Generation
The application processes entered financial information to generate a suggested budget.

### 5.4 Spending Analysis
The application helps users understand how their money is distributed across different expense categories.

### 5.5 Savings Suggestions
The application can provide suggestions for identifying unnecessary expenses and improving savings habits.

### 5.6 Goal-Based Financial Planning
Users can specify financial goals, such as building an emergency fund, to provide context for financial analysis.

### 5.7 Monthly Reports
The application can generate a financial summary to help users review their income, expenses, and savings.

### 5.8 AI-Assisted Guidance
When properly configured, Gemini AI can help generate responses and financial insights based on the information provided.

### 5.9 Rule-Based Fallback
Selected workflows can use local rule-based logic when AI functionality is unavailable or not configured.

### 5.10 Optional Google Sheets Integration
The project includes support for optional Google Sheets synchronization through a Google Apps Script web application.

